The Originals, my fav' show. &lt;3 Davina &lt;3 Klaus &lt;3 Rebekah &lt;3 #Jaiden &lt;3

&amp;#x200B;

Well... I don't agree about TP. In ANY shows you may see characters making phone calls to NPCs, let's use Grey's Anatomy per example, it's pretty common. The point of that scene was that she valuated Ali's words of keeping in contact with people... It could even be Lucas on the call... What they talked about was just details, like easter-eggs. Make no difference to new viewers, nor to the show's plot. :)

About the Ali and Mona's fake death, semantics... A simple Google search on both characters would allow new viewers to read their profile and backstory in quite less than 10 minutes. That'd just make them more interesting. They don't need to be in PLL to get to know them, just like Mss. Hotchkiss is so familiar with Alison by searching about her. :)

&amp;#x200B;

The Orginals itself did A LOT of that too... Marcel commenting of Klaus'es good mood after he had sex with Caroline in TVD and came back in town all happy... Klaus commenting about the otherside collapsing (on TVD), Klaus, Elijah and Rebekah indirectly mentioning characters like Katherine, Elena, Caroline, Bonnie (new viewers wouldn't know who they were, and that also would not make any difference to the plot)... Like on TP, it also didn't make any difference to the plot, nor any difference to new viewers, it was just easter eggs for old fans to be like "awww"... Just like they're doing with The Perfectionists, or likewise, with Legacies, with easter eggs from both TVD and The Originals. :)

Kai and Vallerie come from the same bloodline. Part of the same coven. Val didn't have to deal with her covens things because she killed herself. So as for Kai after he became its leader. 

&amp;#x200B;

In this specific case, no other witches could be a part of the Gemini coven, pretty much because it respects a singular lineage of bloodline. Pretty much as if we'd be about to consider Mikaelson lineage or Bennett lineage as covens... Seems the same, other witches would not be "a part of it" due to the same very fact.
